aption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_04-960x960.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/john-lennon/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_05/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_05-200x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"John Lennon £5 coin, Royal Mint 2025\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_05-200x200.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_05-580x580.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_05-960x960.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_05-768x768.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_05.jpg 1500w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"128798\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/john-lennon/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_05/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_05.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1500,1500\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"John Lennon £5 coin, Royal Mint 2025\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_05-960x960.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/john-lennon/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_08/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_08-200x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"John Lennon UK 1kg Silver Proof Colour Coin box, Royal Mint 2025\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_08-200x200.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_08-580x580.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_08-960x960.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_08-768x768.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_08.jpg 1500w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"128800\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/john-lennon/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_08/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_08.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1500,1500\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"John Lennon UK 1kg Silver Proof Colour Coin box, Royal Mint 2025\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_08-960x960.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/john-lennon/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_09/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_09-200x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"John Lennon UK 1kg Silver Proof Colour Coin box, Royal Mint 2025\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_09-200x200.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_09-580x580.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_09-960x960.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_09-768x768.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_09.jpg 1500w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"128801\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/john-lennon/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_09/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_09.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1500,1500\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"John Lennon UK 1kg Silver Proof Colour Coin box, Royal Mint 2025\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-royal-mint-coin_09-960x960.jpg\"></a></div></figure></div><p>Here’s the full press release:</p><blockquote><div>John Lennon’s legacy is set to be immortalised on a UK commemorative coin by The Royal Mint. The new coin celebrating Lennon’s life and record-breaking career as an artist coincides with the year in which he would have celebrated his 85th birthday.<p></p><p>The coin’s design features a portrait of John Lennon and is based on an image taken by Bob Gruen – one of the most respected photographers in the music industry. It depicts a side profile shot of Lennon, taken on the roof of his penthouse in New York City.</p><p>Experienced coin designer Henry Gray incorporated the portrait of Lennon to feature at the centre of the coins design. John Lennon’s name appears to the left of the portrait while the word ‘Imagine’ features on the right side of the design – a special nod to the artist’s single and album.</p><p>Rebecca Morgan, Director of Commemorative Coin at The Royal Mint said, “Arguably one of the greatest singers and songwriters of all time, Lennon’s achievements as an artist, activist and advocate for peace continues to live on and will now be forever remembered on a coin. Lennon’s portrait has been captured in meticulous detail and in a fitting tribute will be released in the year which the artist would have celebrated his 85th birthday. Still admired by millions of people and generations worldwide, we hope this coin and its design will be treasured for many years to come.”</p><p>John Lennon is the next music artist to form part of The Royal Mint’s ongoing ‘Music Legends’ coin series, celebrating the greatest singer and songwriters in British history. Lennon follows the likes of Queen, David Bowie, Shirley Bassey and Paul McCartney in being honoured on their very own UK coin.</p><p>As a founder of The Beatles and also a solo artist, Lennon has won seven GRAMMY® Awards, including two Lifetime Achievement Awards, Five BRIT Awards including two Special Awards for Outstanding Contribution to Music, 21 NME Awards, 15 Ivor Novellos and an Oscar (Academy Award). He has been inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame and the Songwriters Hall of Fame and has a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame. In 2008, Rolling Stone ranked Lennon in the Top 5 of the magazine’s “100 Greatest Singers Of All Time” list.</p><p>John Lennon fans and collectors will have their opportunity to secure a coin on 17th March at 9am when the full collection becomes available via The Royal Mint’s website. Prices of the coin start at £18.50 and will be available in a range of precious metals with also colour editions of the coin also available exclusively from The Royal Mint.</p></div></blockquote>\n<!--[googlesitekit-end-of-content]--><div style=\"font-size: 12px; margin: 10px 0 10px 0;\"><strong>Page last updated:</strong> 11 August 2025</div></div></div><div class=\"on-this-day-wrapper\"><h3>Also on this day...</h3><ul><li>2009: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2009/03/13/capitol-records-boss-alan-livingston-dies/\">Former Capitol Records boss Alan Livingston dies at 91</a></li><li>1999: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1999/03/13/ringo-starr-all-starr-band-live-hard-rock-hotel-casino-las-vegas/\">Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Hard Rock Hotel &amp; Casino, Las Vegas</a></li><li>1993: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1993/03/13/paul-mccartney-live-adelaide-oval-adelaide/\">Paul McCartney live: Adelaide Oval, Adelaide</a></li><li>1990: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1990/03/13/paul-mccartney-live-tokyo-dome-tokyo-6/\">Paul McCartney live: Tokyo Dome, Tokyo</a></li><li>1981: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1981/03/13/us-single-release-watching-the-wheels-john-lennon/\">US single release: Watching The Wheels by John Lennon</a></li><li>1975: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1975/03/13/recording-treat-her-gently-lonely-old-people-wings-3/\">Recording: Treat Her Gently/Lonely Old People by Wings</a></li><li>1973: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1973/03/13/recording-im-the-greatest-ringo-starr/\">Recording: I’m The Greatest by Ringo Starr</a></li><li>1972: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1972/03/13/recording-tragedy-wings/\">Recording: Tragedy by Wings</a></li><li>1970: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1970/03/13/mixing-sentimental-journey-ringo-starr-3/\">Mixing: Sentimental Journey by Ringo Starr</a></li><li>1969: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1969/03/13/mixing-ive-got-a-feeling-dig-it-maggie-mae-shake-rattle-and-roll-kansas-city-miss-ann-lawdy-miss-clawdy-blue-suede-shoes-you-really-got-a-hold-on-me/\">Mixing: I’ve Got A Feeling, Dig It, Maggie Mae, Shake Rattle And Roll, Kansas City, Miss Ann, Lawdy Miss Clawdy, Blue Suede Shoes, You Really Got A Hold On Me</a></li><li>1967: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1967/03/13/recording-good-morning-good-morning-2/\">Recording: Good Morning Good Morning</a></li><li>1965: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1965/03/13/travel-london-austria/\">Travel: London to Austria</a></li><li>1964: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1964/03/13/mixing-komm-gib-mir-deine-hand-sie-liebt-dich/\">Mixing: Komm, Gib Mir Deine Hand, Sie Liebt Dich</a></li><li>1964: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1964/03/13/filming-a-hard-days-night-10/\">Filming: A Hard Day’s Night</a></li><li>1963: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1963/03/13/live-rialto-theatre-york-2/\">The Beatles live: Rialto Theatre, York</a></li><li>1963: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1963/03/13/recording-mixing-thank-you-girl/\">Recording, mixing: Thank You Girl</a></li><li>1962: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1962/03/13/live-cavern-club-liverpool-151/\">The Beatles live: Cavern Club, Liverpool (lunchtime)</a></li><li>1961: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1961/03/13/live-liverpool-jazz-society-liverpool-3/\">The Beatles live: Liverpool Jazz Society, Liverpool</a></li><li>1961: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1961/03/13/live-cavern-club-liverpool-7/\">The Beatles live: Cavern Club, Liverpool (lunchtime)</a></li><li>1958: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1958/03/13/live-morgue-skiffle-cellar-liverpool/\">The Quarrymen live: Morgue Skiffle Cellar, Liverpool</a></li></ul><p>Want more? Visit the <a title=\"Day after day: the Beatles' history\" href=\"/history/\">Beatles history section</a>.</p></div>",
  "textContent": "The Royal Mint has launched a range of official Paul McCartney gold and silver coins in the UK. It comes just three months after a similar range bearing the image of Paul McCartney.There are 11 items available, ranging from an uncirculated £5 costing £18.50, to a 2oz gold proof coin, limited to 90 copies and costing £7,520. The full range can be purchased from the Royal Mint website.\n\n\n\n£5 Brilliant uncirculated coin, £18.50£5 brilliant uncirculated colour coin, edition of 10,000, £29.501KG silver proof colour coin, edition of 64, £2,9841/40oz gold proof coin, edition of 1,250, £1201oz silver proof colour coin, edition of 5,000, £1232oz silver proof coin, edition of 500, £2255oz silver proof coin, edition of 250, £5451/4oz gold proof coin, edition of 750, £99510oz silver proof colour coin, edition of 150, £1,1651oz gold proof coin, edition of 400, £3,8152oz gold proof coin, edition of 90, £7,520\n\n\n\n\n\nHere’s the full press release:John Lennon’s legacy is set to be immortalised on a UK commemorative coin by The Royal Mint. The new coin celebrating Lennon’s life and record-breaking career as an artist coincides with the year in which he would have celebrated his 85th birthday.The coin’s design features a portrait of John Lennon and is based on an image taken by Bob Gruen – one of the most respected photographers in the music industry. It depicts a side profile shot of Lennon, taken on the roof of his penthouse in New York City.Experienced coin designer Henry Gray incorporated the portrait of Lennon to feature at the centre of the coins design. John Lennon’s name appears to the left of the portrait while the word ‘Imagine’ features on the right side of the design – a special nod to the artist’s single and album.Rebecca Morgan, Director of Commemorative Coin at The Royal Mint said, “Arguably one of the greatest singers and songwriters of all time, Lennon’s achievements as an artist, activist and advocate for peace continues to live on and will now be forever remembered on a coin. Lennon’s portrait has been captured in meticulous detail and in a fitting tribute will be released in the year which the artist would have celebrated his 85th birthday. Still admired by millions of people and generations worldwide, we hope this coin and its design will be treasured for many years to come.”John Lennon is the next music artist to form part of The Royal Mint’s ongoing ‘Music Legends’ coin series, celebrating the greatest singer and songwriters in British history. Lennon follows the likes of Queen, David Bowie, Shirley Bassey and Paul McCartney in being honoured on their very own UK coin.As a founder of The Beatles and also a solo artist, Lennon has won seven GRAMMY® Awards, including two Lifetime Achievement Awards, Five BRIT Awards including two Special Awards for Outstanding Contribution to Music, 21 NME Awards, 15 Ivor Novellos and an Oscar (Academy Award). He has been inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame and the Songwriters Hall of Fame and has a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame. In 2008, Rolling Stone ranked Lennon in the Top 5 of the magazine’s “100 Greatest Singers Of All Time” list.John Lennon fans and collectors will have their opportunity to secure a coin on 17th March at 9am when the full collection becomes available via The Royal Mint’s website. Prices of the coin start at £18.50 and will be available in a range of precious metals with also colour editions of the coin also available exclusively from The Royal Mint.\nPage last updated: 11 August 2025Also on this day...2009: Former Capitol Records boss Alan Livingston dies at 911999: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Hard Rock Hotel & Casino, Las Vegas1993: Paul McCartney live: Adelaide Oval, Adelaide1990: Paul McCartney live: Tokyo Dome, Tokyo1981: US single release: Watching The Wheels by John Lennon1975: Recording: Treat Her Gently/Lonely Old People by Wings1973: Recording: I’m The Greatest by Ringo Starr1972: Recording: Tragedy by Wings1970: Mixing: Sentimental Journey by Ringo Starr1969: Mixing: I’ve Got A Feeling, Dig It, Maggie Mae, Shake Rattle And Roll, Kansas City, Miss Ann, Lawdy Miss Clawdy, Blue Suede Shoes, You Really Got A Hold On Me1967: Recording: Good Morning Good Morning1965: Travel: London to Austria1964: Mixing: Komm, Gib Mir Deine Hand, Sie Liebt Dich1964: Filming: A Hard Day’s Night1963: The Beatles live: Rialto Theatre, York1963: Recording, mixing: Thank You Girl1962: The Beatles live: Cavern Club, Liverpool (lunchtime)1961: The Beatles live: Liverpool Jazz Society, Liverpool1961: The Beatles live: Cavern Club, Liverpool (lunchtime)1958: The Quarrymen live: Morgue Skiffle Cellar, LiverpoolWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
